 "best_idea": "Score each enemy by the damage it can do to you, cut by the distance it must walk and discounted when it draws a counter; attack the highest-scoring enemy you can already hit, and when none is in reach, walk toward the one with the most threat per step.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "Keep the threat score as the one formula that the target pick, the slot pick and the walk-to pick share, since it gives the engine an explicit rule for many-on-one; drop the turn-based cell distance (use ticks to reach) and the archer-blocking sum, since Frankendom is real-time with MAX_ATTACKERS = 3 and has no cell grid in a duel.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A server test with three attackers and one free slot gives the slot to the attacker with the highest threat; an enemy that cannot evade (archer, immovable, or slower walker) is chosen before a flyer with a higher threat; a double-attacking enemy with a counter scores below the same enemy without one."
